---
const steps = [
  {
    name: "Intent",
    who: "A person",
    person: true,
    body: "“Text customers when their order ships. Respect opt-outs. Only text verified numbers.”",
  },
  {
    name: "Plan",
    who: "Planning agent",
    body: "Asks the map what's involved: orders already publishes OrderShipped, notifications sends email, user-preferences holds opt-outs, and there's no SMS provider yet.",
  },
  {
    name: "Token",
    who: "Token service",
    body: "Write access to the internals of notifications, read access to OrderShipped and UserPreferences, network access only to the SMS provider's test endpoint.",
  },
  {
    name: "Build",
    who: "Coding agent",
    body: "Writes code and tests in a disposable environment seeded with fake customers.",
  },
  {
    name: "Escalate",
    who: "Coding agent, then judge",
    body: "UserPreferences can't say whether a number is verified. The agent escalates with a failing test and the map path; the judge confirms the new optional field is additive and grants it.",
  },
  {
    name: "Apply",
    who: "Coding agent",
    body: "Submits an application: about 1,400 lines, summarized as four changes in meaning.",
  },
  {
    name: "Route",
    who: "Classifier",
    body: "Sends it to a person, because a new outside vendor will receive customers' phone numbers.",
  },
  {
    name: "Verify",
    who: "Judge",
    body: "Re-runs the tests in a fresh environment, confirms the opt-out check exists, and confirms nothing else writes to customer data.",
  },
  {
    name: "Review",
    who: "A person",
    person: true,
    body: "Reads a one-page summary and approves in minutes. Their attention goes to the vendor and the data flow, not to 1,400 lines.",
  },
  {
    name: "Roll out",
    who: "Production",
    body: "Ships to a small share of customers first. Delivery errors and opt-out complaints feed back into the classifier and the agent's track record.",
  },
];
---

<section class="section wrap lifecycle" aria-labelledby="lifecycle-title">
  <h2 class="section-title" id="lifecycle-title">One feature, end to end.</h2>
  <p class="prose lead">
    Here is the manifesto's example feature traveling through Onus: send customers a text message when
    their order ships.
  </p>

  <ol class="timeline">
    {
      steps.map((s, i) => (
        <li class={`strip step ${s.person ? "is-person" : ""}`}>
          <span class="t-n" aria-hidden="true">{i + 1}</span>
          <p class="t-name">{s.name}</p>
          <p class="t-body">{s.body}</p>
          <p class="t-who">{s.who}</p>
        </li>
      ))
    }
  </ol>

  <p class="takeaway">
    Notice where human attention went: one sentence of intent at the start, one decision about a vendor near
    the end. Everything in between was done by agents and checked by machines, with evidence at every step.
  </p>
</section>

<style>
  .lead {
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }

  .timeline {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 2.5rem 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.4rem;
  }

  .step {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 2.75rem 8rem 1fr 11rem;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 1rem;
    padding: 0.85rem 1.1rem 0.85rem 0.75rem;
  }

  .t-n {
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    font-stretch: 120%;
    font-weight: 800;
    line-height: 1;
  }

  .t-name {
    font-weight: 700;
    font-stretch: 110%;
  }

  .t-body {
    font-size: 0.9875rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .t-who {
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    font-stretch: 82%;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--ink-2);
    text-align: right;
  }

  .is-person .t-who {
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .takeaway {
    margin-top: 2rem;
    font-size: clamp(1.25rem, 1rem + 1vw, 1.6rem);
    font-stretch: 106%;
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.3;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    max-width: 40ch;
  }

  @media (max-width: 52rem) {
    .step {
      grid-template-columns: 2.25rem 1fr;
      gap: 0.2rem 0.75rem;
    }

    .t-n {
      grid-row: span 3;
    }

    .t-who {
      text-align: left;
      order: -1;
      grid-column: 2;
    }

    .t-name,
    .t-body {
      grid-column: 2;
    }
  }
</style>
